<statement>
<p>It is estimated that 57<percent/> of Kickstarter projects are successfully funded. Assume each Kickstarter project is independent. A random sample of 19 Kickstarter projects are followed. Let <m>\displaystyle{X}</m> be the number Kickstarter projects that are successfully funded. Calculate the following:</p>
<p>a. <m>\displaystyle\mu_{{X}}</m>: <fillin characters="4" /></p>
<p>b. <m>\displaystyle\sigma_{{X}}</m>: <fillin characters="4" /></p>
<p>c. <m>\displaystyle{P}{\left({X}={10}\right)}</m>: <fillin characters="4" /></p>
<p>d. <m>\displaystyle{P}{\left({X}{<}{13}\right)}</m>: <fillin characters="4" /></p>
<p>e. <m>\displaystyle{P}{\left({X}{>}{10}\right)}</m>: <fillin characters="4" /></p>
<p>f.  <m>\displaystyle{P}{\left({X}\geq{10}\right)}</m>: <fillin characters="4" /></p>
<p>g. <m>\displaystyle{P}{\left({9}\leq{X}\leq{12}\right)}</m>: <fillin characters="20" /></p>

</statement>
<answer>
<p><ul><li>10.83</li><li>2.1579851714041</li><li>0.16808664640139</li><li>0.77865932235494</li><li>0.56474518940741</li><li>0.73283183831631</li><li>0.638293368089</li></ul></p>
</answer>

